James sought a story for his 5-year-old son, Austin, who enjoys scary themes like vampires and monsters but finds typical early reader books too sappy. He wanted an engaging narrative with a bad guy protagonist and trickery, tailored for Austin’s reading level—short words and repetitions. James requested a structured 4-page book format, with four lines for him to read per page and corresponding lines for Austin. The goal was to create an exciting story that resonated with Austin's interests while being suitable for his reading skills.
